<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n18372" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flexŭōsus</span></b> , a,
		um, adj.
		2. flexus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>full of turns</i> or <i>windings</i>,
				<i>tortuous</i>, <i>flexuous</i>,
				<i>crooked</i>, <i>winding.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flexuosum iter habet auditus, ne quid intrare
					possit,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cic. N. D. 2, 57, 144</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Taurus mons,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 27, 27, § 98</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">volatus hirundini,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					10, 24, 35</span></i>
			,  § 73.—<i>Sup.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">intestina flexuosissimis orbibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					11, 37, 79, § 200</span></i>
			.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">fraudes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Cath. 6, 143</span></i>
			.—* <i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">flexu-ōse</span></b> , <i>tortuously</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">si flexuose volitet flamma,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 35, 84, § 357</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
